.TH CBMAP_INIT_MP 3 "2026-09-20" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Macros"
.SH NAME
cbmap_init_mp \- create an ordered map with a custom allocator into an already declared handle
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ccollections/cbstmap.h>

cbmap_init_mp(hm_name, mmgmt_procs);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Creates an ordered map that takes all of its memory from mmgmt_procs. The
macro then assigns that map to hm_name. The caller must declare the handle
first, with cbmap_declare(3) or cbmap_declare_scoped(3). The key type and
the value type do not come to this macro as arguments. The macro reads them
from the companion type variables that the declare macro created.

The macro is cbmap_init(3) plus an allocator. It uses the default order for
the declared key type. cbmap_init_cc(3) replaces the order instead, and
cbmap_init_full(3) takes both.

The one-step equivalents are cbmap_construct_mp(3) and
cbmap_construct_mp_scoped(3).
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
hm_name      The map handle that the caller declared before. The macro
             creates the map into it
mmgmt_procs  Pointer to a ccol_memmgmt_procs_t, or NULL for the default
             allocator
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
None. This macro expands to a statement and does not expand to an
expression.
.fi
.SH NOTES
.nf
The macro stops the program through ccol_fatal_err() if the creation fails
All four members of ccol_memmgmt_procs_t must not be NULL
The map copies the procedures into itself. The ccol_memmgmt_procs_t of
the caller therefore does not have to outlive the call. But the procedures
themselves must stay callable for the whole life of the map
Every tree node that the map allocates later comes from these procedures.
Everything that the map frees goes back to them
The allocator has no effect on the order. The declared key type decides
the order, as cbmap_create_full(3) describes. The walk goes in ascending
key order
.fi
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
ccol_memmgmt_procs_t procs = {
    .malloc = my_malloc, .calloc = my_calloc,
    .realloc = my_realloc, .free = my_free,
};

cbmap_declare(sorted, int, char *);
cbmap_init_mp(sorted, &procs);
int k = 42;
cbmap_insert(sorted, k, "hello");
cbmap_destroy(sorted);
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR cbmap_init (3),
.BR cbmap_init_cc (3),
.BR cbmap_init_full (3),
.BR cbmap_declare (3),
.BR cbmap_construct_mp (3),
.BR cbmap_create_full (3),
.BR cbmap_destroy (3)
